                <pb facs="0533" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.796/505: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janerio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-19T14:00:00-03:00">August 19, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1108. My telegram No. 1093, August 16, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">2</hi>]
                        p.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d535-f1"/> The Interventor is here and has seen
                    President Vargas. He says that President Vargas approves in principle the sale
                    of Vasp with the idea of eventually incorporating it into an all-inclusive
                    national Brazilian company.</p>
                <p>The Interventor suggests that the question of price be now taken up. However, as
                    the Department is aware the Washington end of this business is not yet all
                    clear.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
